     ppoorrttssllooggggeerr — logs ports builds selectively

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppoorrttssllooggggeerr [--ss] _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ppoorrttssllooggggeerr saves logs from ports build in separate files.

     ppoorrttssllooggggeerr handles directory change messages from the ports tree infra‐
     structure and switches to a corresponding log file situated in _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y
     accordingly, e.g., it will log the build from screen in
     _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y_/_s_c_r_e_e_n_-_4_._0_._3_p_1_._l_o_g.  ppoorrttssllooggggeerr will filter progress-bar noise
     from ftp(1), pkg_add(1), and pkg_create(1).

     By default, ppoorrttssllooggggeerr acts as a filter and still passes its input to
     stdout, unless run with --ss.

     It is most often used as

           $ make package 2>&1 | portslogger logdir

     or in conjunction with tmux(1), such as

           $ tmux pipe-pane 'portslogger -s logdir'

